exports[`screen: 'help apps install' > en 40 color 1`] = `
"  bladecp apps install <server> <app>
 ━━━━━━━━━━━━──────────────────────────
  Installs an app on one of the domains
  of a server. On a terminal it asks
  first; the install itself runs on
  BladeCP and takes a few minutes.

  Usage ────────────────────────────────
  bladecp apps install <server> <app>
      [--domain <host>]
      [--app-version <version>]
      [--option <id>=<value>] ...
      [--yes]

  Arguments ───────────────────────────
  <server>   The server: its ID, or its
             first characters (at least
             4).
  <app>      The app, as bladecp apps
             list shows it (for example
             wordpress).

  Options ─────────────────────────────
  --domain <host>
    Domain of the server to install it
    on (the main one when left out)
  --app-version <version>
    Version to install (the recommended
    one when left out)
  --option <id>=<value>
    A setting of the app as name=value
    (repeat for each one)
  -y, --yes
    Do not ask before installing on a
    terminal

  On a terminal it asks for the
  settings you did not give. In
  scripts, give each one with --option
  name=value (bladecp apps show <app>
  lists them). The language follows the
  CLI and the administrator email is
  the one of your account, unless you
  choose others.

  Examples ────────────────────────────
  › bladecp apps install 0197a1c4
    wordpress
    Install WordPress, answering the
    questions
  › bladecp apps install 0197a1c4
    wordpress --domain blog.example.com
    --option admin_user=maria --option
    site_title="Maria's blog" --yes
    Install WordPress without
    questions, for scripts

  Global options ──────────────────────
  --json
    Print machine-readable JSON (no
    colors, no prompts)
  --api-url <url>
    API address (default
    https://api.bladecp.com)
  --lang <en|pt-BR|es>
    Language for messages
  --debug
    Describe each request on stderr
    (the key is never shown)
  --verbose
    Same as --debug
  -h, --help
    Show help
  -v, --version
    Show the version

  See also  bladecp apps show <app> ·
  bladecp domains add <server> <host>

